<title>INDIA: Indian car, truck output rose in March - AIAM. [CORRECTED 11:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>Indian car, truck output rose in March - AIAM. [CORRECTED 11:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 36,286 cars in March, up from 35,228 in the same month in 1996, the Association of Indian Automobile Manufacturers (AIAM) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>AIAM said in a statement that production of light and heavy trucks rose to 32,212 units in March from 27,900 in the same month in 1996.  </p>
<p> AUTOMOBILE PRODUCTION &amp; SALES	  (number of units)</p>
<p>   Category			 PRODUCTION</p>
<p>		     Mar 97  Mar 96  Mar 95  Apr96-Mar97 Apr95-Mar96</p>
<p>   TRUCKS	  32,212  27,900  22,173    303,017     259,090</p>
<p>   CARS	    36,286  35,228  29,561    404,040     348,240</p>
<p>   2-WHEELERS   258,629 268,953 220,157  2,979,227   2,656,017</p>
<p>					SALES</p>
<p>		     Mar 97  Mar 96  Mar 95  Apr96-Mar97 Apr95-Mar96</p>
<p>   TRUCKS	  40,127  31,963  27,152    296,955     257,092</p>
<p>   CARS	    42,751  39,163  33,674    411,305     345,340</p>
<p>(Corrects total Apr96-Mar97 car sales from 406,241.)</p>
<p>   2-WHEELERS   274,739 271,399 223,503  2,963,497   2,658,288</p>
<p>Source: Association of Indian Automobile Manufacturers</p>
<p>--New Delhi Newsroom +91-11 301-2024</p>
